# PIG and ThumbSet are licensed for nonprofit academic use and their download
# page says explicitly: do NOT transfer this dataset to others. Committing
# them to a public repository is transferring them, so they never go in git.
PianoFingeringDataset*/
ThumbSet*/
FingeringFiles/
*_fingering.txt
!tests/fixtures/pig/*_fingering.txt

# Our own fingering annotations. These are a held-out test set, and keeping
# them out of the repo makes it harder to train on them by accident.
data/

# weights_learned.json IS committed on purpose. It is 99 numbers that our own
# model learned, not any part of PIG: no fingering, note or piece can be
# recovered from it, so publishing it is not transferring the dataset. The
# backend loads it at startup, so the app needs it to serve the trained model.
